<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         THE APP THEME'S BRUSH + METRIC LAYER, BY SECTION.

         Every `x:Key` this file used to declare inline now lives in
         `Styles/Resources/`, moved byte for byte. Each part is a `<Styles>`
         carrying nothing but its own `<Styles.Resources>` — the same shape
         `Styles/FireTokens.axaml` has always had, which is what proves the
         keys still resolve app-wide from this depth.

         ORDER IS THE CONTRACT. A resource dictionary merged later wins, so
         these includes stand in the exact order the sections stood in the
         one file. Every key here is UNIQUE (a duplicate `x:Key` crashes the
         app at `App.Initialize()`), so nothing depends on the tie-break
         today — which is precisely why a shuffle would be silent.

         COLOURS still live in `App.axaml`'s `Application.Resources`, where
         `ThemeService` mutates them; everything here is the BRUSH layer over
         them and reaches them by `{DynamicResource}`, across the dictionary
         boundary, exactly as it always did.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Resources/ThemeSurfaces.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Resources/HardwareMaterials.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Resources/Metrics.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Resources/FluentOverrides.axaml" />

</Styles>
